Abstract
Finite-context modeling is a powerful tool for compressing and hence for representing DNA
sequences. We describe an algorithm to detect genomic regularities, within a blind discovery
strategy. The algorithm uses information profiles built using suitable combinations of finitecontext models. We used the genome of the fission yeast Schizosaccharomyces pombe strain
