Graphical representations of DNA sequences are a handy way of quickly finding regions of potential interest. This has been a topic addressed using various approaches
(see, for example, [1–10]), some of them relying on information theoretical principles.
Both global and local estimates of the randomness of a sequence provide useful information, but both also have shortcomings. Global estimates do not show how the
