We propose a new scheme for individual addressing of trapped ion qubits, selecting them via
their motional frequency. We show that geometric phase gates can perform single-qubit rotations
using the coherent interference of spin-independent and (global) spin-dependent forces. The spinindependent forces, which can be generated via localised electric fields, increase the gate speed
while reducing its sensitivity to motional decoherence, which we show analytically and numerically.
While the scheme applies to most trapped ion experimental setups, we numerically simulate a specific
laser-free implementation, showing cross-talk errors below 10−6 for reasonable parameters.

