derivation of laws governing natural phenomena.
Recently, Large Language Models (LLMs) have
gained interest for this task due to their potential to leverage embedded scientific knowledge
for hypothesis generation. However, it is difficult to assess the true discovery capabilities of
these methods because existing benchmarks often use well-known equations. This makes them
vulnerable to memorization by LLMs and results
in inflated performance metrics that do not reflect genuine discovery. In this paper, we introduce LLM-SRBench, a comprehensive benchmark with 239 challenging problems across four
scientific domains specifically designed to evaluate LLM-based scientific equation discovery
methods while preventing trivial memorization.
